-- title:
--   Integrality of the degeneracy substitution q↦ q^ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $N,M$ be nonzero natural numbers, let $\ell$ be a prime, and assume $N\ell \mid M$. Here, for a level $N$, `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set `divisorExpansions N`, and `laurentBaseChange L` of such a field is the intermediate field of $L$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of that field under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb L`. The map `towerSubstBar L N ℓ h` is the $L$-algebra homomorphism from `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` to `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull M)` obtained as the substitution map `heckeBetaBar L N ℓ` (given on Laurent series by $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, with target the base-changed level-$N\ell$ field) followed by `towerInclBar L h`, the inclusion of intermediate fields coming from the containment of the base-changed level-$N\ell$ field in the base-changed level-$M$ field. The assertion is that the ring homomorphism underlying this $L$-algebra map is integral: every element of the level-$M$ field is a root of a monic polynomial with coefficients in the image.
--
--   This is the integrality of the degeneracy map $\tau \mapsto \ell\tau$ from level $N$ into any level divisible by $N\ell$, for $\ell$ prime, in the function-field model of the modular tower. It is used throughout the analysis of places and specialisations of the modular correspondences, where integrality of the two degeneracy maps lets one extend valuations and control reductions along the tower.
